#. settings-schema.json->use-https->description
msgid "Encrypted (HTTPS, port 8443)"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->use-https->tooltip
msgid ""
"Talks to AutarkTrade over HTTPS and trusts only the server certificate you "
"paired below. Without it the API key and your account data travel "
"unencrypted. The port above (8080) is still used to fetch the certificate "
"when pairing."
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->https-port->description
msgid "HTTPS port"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-fetch->description
msgid "1. Fetch server certificate"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-fetch->tooltip
msgid ""
"Fetches the AutarkTrade CA over http://host:port/api/esp32/ca and shows its "
"SHA-256 fingerprint below."
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-pending->description
msgid "Fingerprint to compare"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-pending->tooltip
msgid ""
"Must match Settings  General  HTTPS in the AutarkTrade web app. Only then "
"confirm."
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-confirm->description
msgid "2. Fingerprint matches  pair"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-confirm->tooltip
msgid ""
"Stores the certificate (0600) next to the desklet settings. From then on "
"only this certificate is trusted."
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-paired->description
msgid "Paired certificate (SHA-256)"
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->ca-paired->tooltip
msgid ""
"Empty = not paired. If the server certificate changes, pair again with the "
"two buttons above."
msgstr ""

#. settings-schema.json->server-port->tooltip
msgid ""
"Default: 8080 (HTTP). With HTTPS on it is only used to fetch the certificate "
"when pairing."
msgstr ""

